      "writtenOn": "2026-05-29T17:51:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "EMSGSIZE occurs when attempting to write a large multi-event batch that exceeds the total socket buffer capacity. Inside threadMain, we are flushing the congested events one-by-one (batch size of 1). A single display event is only 104 bytes, which is far below the socket capacity. Individual writes will therefore never trigger EMSGSIZE. Any other unexpected failure results in the connection being removed from EventThread, so explicit EMSGSIZE handling is not needed here.",
      "parentUuid": "9c867c60_8d406170",
      "revId": "0ebc75933b794102751931112b206be7730debb8",
