      "writtenOn": "2026-05-29T17:51:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "EAGAIN is returned when the socket buffer is temporarily full (congestion). EMSGSIZE is returned when the batch size of a bulk write exceeds the socket buffer capacity (e.g. writing all 180 refresh rates at once). In both cases, the events are safely queued in heap memory. Inside threadMain, we flush them one-by-one (size of 1). Single event writes are only 104 bytes, meaning they will never trigger EMSGSIZE. Thus, we only need to retry on EAGAIN (if the socket is still full). Any other error is treated as fatal and results in connection clean-up.",
      "parentUuid": "6479d673_8016b92f",
      "revId": "0ebc75933b794102751931112b206be7730debb8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
