      "writtenOn": "2026-05-29T17:51:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. Extracted the congestion queueing logic into a helper method queueIfCongestedLocked. Regarding SUPPORTED_REFRESH_RATE: During display config changes, SurfaceFlinger posts the list of all supported refresh rates in bulk. On high-refresh-rate displays, this list easily overflows the non-blocking socket buffer (4KB), resulting in EAGAIN or EMSGSIZE. Treating these events as critical ensures they are not silently dropped, preventing display settings app desync. Standard VSYNC events are not critical and are never queued.",
      "parentUuid": "d4a5b98a_6aaa6739",
      "revId": "0ebc75933b794102751931112b206be7730debb8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
